*1.) Privacy Notice:*

[~accountid:63622ea17d4645af4f03bd18] besides a description of the applicable safeguards (letter F of point 3 of the rules) the requirements are similar to the GDPR. 


*Content of the privacy notice: https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/rulebook/data-3-information-be-provided-data-subjects*

(A) the identity and contact details of the [_Data Controller_|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Data%20Controller];
(B) the purposes of the intended [_Processing_|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Processing] and the lawful basis for that [_Processing_|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Processing], as set out in [Article 10|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/node/13515] of the Regulations;
(C) whether the [_Data Subject_|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Data%20Subject] is obliged to provide the [_Personal Data_|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Personal%20Data] and the possible consequences of failing to do so;
(D) the categories of [_Personal Data_|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Personal%20Data] concerned;
(E) if the data are to be, or may be, disclosed to one or more other individuals or entities, their names or a description of their categories;
(F) if the [_Data Controller_|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Data%20Controller] intends to transfer the data to another jurisdiction, a statement of that fact, setting out a description of the applicable safeguards and, if applicable, how and where to obtain a copy of the safeguards;
(G) if the [_Processing_|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Processing] is based on the legitimate interests of the [_Data Controller_|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Data%20Controller] or another [_Person_ |https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Person%C2%A0][ to whom the data are disclosed or to comply with an obligation imposed on the Data Controller|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/to%20whom%20the%20data%20are%20disclosed%20or%20to%20comply%20with%20an%20obligation%20imposed%20on%20the%20Data%20Controller] by law, a clear statement of those interests or obligations;
(H) the period for which the data will be retained, or how to determine that period;
(I) a statement of the [_Data Subject_|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Data%20Subject]'s right to request from the [_Data Controller_|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Data%20Controller]:(i) access to the data;(ii) rectification of the data;(iii) erasure of the data;(iv) restriction of the [_Processing_|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Processing] of the data;(v) objection to the [_Processing_|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Processing] of the data; and(vi) data portability.
(J) whether automated decision-making will be used, and if so:(i) meaningful information about the logic applied; and(ii) the significance, and the likely consequences, of the decision-making for the [_Data Subject_|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Data%20Subject].
(K) if the [_Processing_|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Processing] is based on consent, that the [_Data Subject_|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Data%20Subject] has the right to withdraw that consent at any time, but that withdrawing the consent does not affect the lawfulness of [_Processing_|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Processing] based on consent before the withdrawal; and
(L) that under [Article 34|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/node/13542] of the Regulations, the [_Data Subject_|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Data%20Subject] has the right to lodge a complaint with the Data Protection Office if the [_Data Subject_|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Data%20Subject] considers that the [_Processing_|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Processing] of [_Personal Data_|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Personal%20Data] relating to them infringes the [_Regulations_|https://qfcra-en.thomsonreuters.com/glossary-tag/Regulations].


*2.) Processing of sensitive data* (Personal Data revealing or relating to race or ethnicity, political affiliation or opinions, religious or philosophical beliefs, trade-union or organisational membership, criminal records, health or sex life, and genetic and *biometric data used to identify an individual*)

We have to check what legal basis we are using for the processing of biometric data (If non of the legal basis in Art 12 (1) is suitable; *we can also can apply for a permit from the Data Protection Office to process Sensitive Personal Data when none of the other options in this article are appropriate.*

*3.) International Data Transfers (No Data Localisation)* Processing of Personal Data that involves the transfer of the Personal Data to a Recipient located in a jurisdiction outside the QFC that the Data Protection Office has decided has an adequate level of protection does not require any specific authorisation or notification to the Data Protection Office.

Right now member states of the European Union are considered as countries with an adequate level of protection   ([https://www.qfc.qa/resource-centre#doccat=1240445d1dd142aaa87dfba6e4c88aa0|https://www.qfc.qa/resource-centre#doccat=1240445d1dd142aaa87dfba6e4c88aa0|smart-link] ) For transfers to other jurisdictions we would need tha QFC contract clauses OR a permission by the local authroity

