Hi [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] as an update here:

* theoretically:
** in all countries: PL, RO, CZ, SK - the relevant local language version is listed in the relevant country section in our legal website; 
** in addition, the Marketplace Guidelines are linked in *PL* t&c and have been accepted during the RH business transfer as of 2023 and will be linked soon in *RO* t&c due to the t&c update mentioned [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/LSS-23473?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNTQxYTQ4ZjAzYjBkNGIyY2FkMWYwMWQzYmZhOWZiYzUiLCJwIjoiaiJ9]; 
** *CZ and SK* are not that consumer/user-sensitive markets, therefore the t&c update can be done in next round changes in due course;
* please note, however, that the content of the Marketplace Guideline can raise the concerns - there is a risk that, in the event of any dispute (either intervention by a consumer protection authority or an individual dispute with a user), the Marketplace Guidelines could be considered unfair or abusive, particularly because:
** violations of the Guidelines trigger blocking, i.e. suspension of the service or even termination of the contract, and although in principle the right to block for misbehaviour is justified, the Guidelines are not clear which cases qualify for blocking, what is the procedure, etc.;
** the user does not receive any warning or so;
** the user has no right of appeal against Bolt's decision;
** it is not clear if Bolt Balance credit is refunded after the account has been blocked.
* These principles derived from EU law, so apply in all countries, only the practical risk of detection and enforcement may vary. It will also depend on our blocking rules in practice - in case of any challenge, we may defend that in practice, we apply the Guidelines only in serious cases (criminal charges, public authorities' requests or similar). 
* To date, however, I have not heard of any challenges or disputes regarding our Guidelines. For full roll-out, however, my recommendation will be to revise the Marketplace Guidelines to address the points above and make them fair and reasonable, as well as tailored to our actual needs.

