Hi [~accountid:6052891645a3bb006808f764] and [~accountid:5b4c96fbda498c2c21cb8544]. As discussed with you both seperately:

* It appears that the relationship between Bolt, Wema Bank, and any other involved Bank is actually one of Independant Controllership. Per Cesar's explanation, we don't share any Driver/customer personal data with Wema directly, *but Wema may receive some data when payment is received from another 3rd party Bank*. 
* I have gone back to look at the current draft contract again which states as follows in Clause 18:

{quote}*18. Data Protection*

18.1. The Company hereby agrees to {{obtain the consent of its customers, riders, partners and the partner's agents to the sharing of the information (including personal information) to be provided to the Bank for the administration and operation of the transaction contemplated under this Agreement}}, and comply with other relevant provisions of the Nigerian Data Protection Regulation, 2019 (NDPR), as well as the Nigerian Data Protection  Act  2023  (NDPA)  and  comply  with  any  directions  made  by  any  competent  regulatory  authority concerning the fulfilment of their respective obligations under this Agreement.

18.2. The Parties herein agree to strictly comply with all applicable privacy and data protection laws, such as the Nigeria  Data  Protection  Regulation  as  well  as  all  other  applicable  regulations  and  directives  in  collecting,
using, processing, handling and/or transferring any of the Confidential Information which may contain any
personal data.{quote}

* {color:#ff5630}*My recommendation is that we go back to Wema and state as follows:*{color}
** {color:#bf2600}We are aligned that typically Wema Bank will not be acting as a Processor for Bolt, and will instead be an Independent Controller.{color}
** {color:#bf2600}Where we are not aligned is on the transfer of data from Bolt to Wema. On further review, we do not believe Bolt will be sharing (whether directly or indirectly) any personal data of customers, riders, partners or their agents with Wema. Wema should kindly explain why they want Bolt to obtain consent from these parties in 18.1 when Bolt is not sharing any of their data with Wema.{color}
** {color:#bf2600}We’d like Wema to confirm that they won't be receiving any personal data directly from Bolt as part of the transactions. {color}
* Once we receive Wema’s feedback, I’ll propose further updates to Clause 18 and close it off.

