Hi [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] [~accountid:609bd1fadafdf0006806ed70] [~accountid:610a3ee66051c5006aeeeea1],

By way of context, the ES RH team does not want to show the breakdown of the prices of RH services to passengers in the user app, i.e. they only want to display a lump sum. 

I was asked whether this is legally possible or whether we are obliged to display the breakdown of prices as we currently do.

After reading the relevant articles of the national law on consumers and users and the regional legislation on consumers and their goods (copied below in green) I understand that we are not obliged to show the breakdown per minute and km but we are obliged to show _the surcharges or discounts, the charges passed on to the consumer and user and the additional charges for ancillary services._

Taking the screenshot attached to this ticket as an example, I would be inclined to think that we are obliged to show (i) the fare, (ii) the waiting time fee and (iii) the cancellation charges; and therefore we could only remove the price per minute and kilometre.

[~accountid:609bd1fadafdf0006806ed70] - I believe you have also looked at the transport regulations and there does not seem to be an obligation to display the price per minute and km.

Eager to hear your opinion

Many thanks!

----


