Hey!

These requests are very common and as a general approach, we comply with them, but try to clarify the scope beforehand.

The SOP should be looking like this:

# The request comes in;
# The scope is checked by the privacy team (there have been some instances where the request is unreasonably vast - like hundreds of thousands of entries; should this be the case, the tax team usually asks for a reduction in scope or prolonging the request);
# The request is reassigned to tax team ([~accountid:62ea2a695111209f4fde8265] or [~accountid:5eda5d0647291b0b8608735a] for the Baltic region);
# They will assemble the requested data and continue the correspondence with the tax authorities;

