The aim of this task is to provide the data and CS teams with ‘*reclassification keywords*’ to track such queries. CS tickets with these keywords will automatically be flagged as ‘reclassification related’ and be escalated to our CS team based in HQ. Doing this will avoid sensitive tickets being answered by external CS teams. 

*Guidance:*

* *Avoid false positives:* We are only looking to ‘tag’ tickets which concern a party asking for employment related benefits. We need to avoid including generic keywords that will flag tickets that do not specifically concern this. For example, the following words are too broad and should not be included: *lawyer, court, blocking, suspension, termination, rights*.
* *Recommended categories of keyword*: 
** words that specifically relate to employment benefits (e.g. pension, minimum wage);
** the name of any relevant legislation;
** the name of any popular driver unions;
** any well known names from case law;
** any words that have significant legal meaning in respect of employment (e.g. subcontracting).
* *Include alternative spellings and abbreviations:* for example, include the full spelling and abbreviated name of any union.

[https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Jm-BnMuB0qqcv3t4RbghennZna6KuIxPDso3a46YO2g/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Jm-BnMuB0qqcv3t4RbghennZna6KuIxPDso3a46YO2g/edit|smart-link]- can you please add the relevant keywords related to the employment relationship, given the above guidance? As an example, in the doc you can find UK and FR keywords. And here is what is proposed for PL [https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FEy0grVVUrtCFI-9OZOfFNyFK1zByROjrSRTmMYAvIc/edit|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FEy0grVVUrtCFI-9OZOfFNyFK1zByROjrSRTmMYAvIc/edit|smart-link] . Thank you!

